Title: Artists fear AI using their talent for free
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Lily Dooner', 'Text': '"What really scares me is the idea that one day I might be watching a film, and hear a voice created out of snippets of mine," she said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 105}}, {'Speaker': 'Lily Dooner', 'Text': '"AI can give you something passable in seconds… for me to give you something it\'s going to be hours of my time," she said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Speaker': 'Lily Dooner', 'Text': '"The difference is AI can\'t give you something incredible. I can."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 59}}, {'Speaker': 'Tim Evans', 'Text': 'The genie is out of the bottle - these models cannot be built and will not be built without hoovering up this vast amount of data.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 54, 'EndChar': 164}}, {'Speaker': 'Tim Evans', 'Text': '"We\'d batted back and forth ideas about creating a two-man show… the idea was forever lost [when Alex died]. That was until, of course, the explosion of AI technology."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 162}}, {'Speaker': 'Tim Evans', 'Text': '"Used in the right way, [AI models] can be used as really powerful, democratizing tools for creativity," he said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 20, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 100}}, {'Speaker': 'Tim Evans', 'Text': '"As yet the compensation question is being left unanswered."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 21, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 54}}, {'Speaker': 'Peter Kyle', 'Text': '"I am offering to look comprehensively at the challenges creatives have into the future," he said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 24, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 94}}, {'Speaker': 'Peter Kyle', 'Text': '"I will give them the rights that they have in the analogue age… fit for the digital age."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 25, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 77}}, {'Speaker': 'Rebecca Farkas', 'Text': '"At the moment the government favours putting the onus on creators to opt out of having their work scraped by AI," said visual artist Rebecca Farkas.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 29, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Speaker': 'Rebecca Farkas', 'Text': '"AI could look at my animations, and then it could copy it in exactly my style… you could put a prompt in to say \'make an animation like Rebecca Farkas\'," she said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 31, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 150}}, {'Speaker': 'Rebecca Farkas', 'Text': '"You\'re helping one industry by taking away from another industry," she said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 34, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 73}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'But her worst fear is finding her own distinctive vocals have been stolen from her by the power of artificial intelligence (AI).', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 109}}, {'Description': 'The Leominster resident, 28, is among artists from Herefordshire who have been telling BBC Politics Midlands that AI poses a risk to their livelihoods without greater copyright protection for their work.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 183}}, {'Description': "Ms Dooner said AI's vast potential – and speed – was already impacting creative industries like her own.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 87}}, {'Description': "But she said the technology's reliance on mimicry would always hold it back.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 71}}, {'Description': 'Tim Evans, artistic director and CEO of Powerhouse, a Herefordshire-based theatre organisation, said: "The genie is out of the bottle - these models cannot be built and will not be built without hoovering up this vast amount of data."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 164}}, {'Description': 'He himself is no enemy of the technology.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 37}}, {'Description': 'After his brother Alex died in 2017, he used the software to recreate his voice for the play Mappa Mundi, external, training the model with dozens of recordings.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 138}}, {'Description': 'But Mr Evans said artists needed to be compensated for their private intellectual property being used.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 19, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 86}}, {'Description': 'She is currently working to turn sketches and drawings into video animation. It is a time-consuming process.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 30, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 89}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Lily poses for a photograph next to her recording and mixing equipment in her bedroom in Leominster. Behind her are shelves of electronic equipment, a tapestry with the Sun, moons and stars, and a guitar.'}]}
